<title>USA: U.S. factory vegoil product use - Census.</title>
<headline>U.S. factory vegoil product use - Census.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. factories used 1,256.4 million lbs of vegoils in October in edible product output versus a revised 1,221.4 million lbs in September and 1,242.3 in October 1995.</p>
<p>U.S. factory vegoil use with refining losses were as follows:</p>
<p>   (Mln Lbs) --    Oct 96  Sept 96     Oct 95</p>
<p>    Soybean Oil  1,169.6   1,073.1     1,125.4</p>
<p> Cottonseed Oil	N/A	N/A	    N/A</p>
<p>Year-to-date oil use with refining losses (Mln Lbs):</p>
<p>				    1996	   1995</p>
<p>		 Soybean Oil  10,514.5     10,612.5</p>
<p>	    Cottonseed Oil	 N/A	    N/A</p>
<p> OUTPUT -- Soybean Crude  12,531.6     12,894.2</p>
<p>		     Refined  10,174.5     10,291.8</p>
<p>	  Cottonseed Crude   1,083.8	    N/A</p>
<p>		     Refined     711.3	  808.0</p>
<p>		  Corn Crude   1,745.3	1,872.5</p>
<p>		     Refined     798.4	  905.4</p>
</text>
